 "logline": "Four days of rain: the girl in Los Angeles, a basement in a storm, a question Laney has been saving, and the Supreme Court deciding while two people argue under one umbrella.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "At Sully’s, Laney, to Lena: “Oh my God. He found a California you. Excuse me while I go be a bitch on your behalf.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "And you, with the whole bar listening: “What is *wrong* with you?”"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the back hall, Lena: “Atlanta. I kept your chair till the half.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the Saab, Skye: “You don’t have to tell me the rest. I can tell there’s a rest.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "Hale, at the seminar table: “Three pages each on why you are wrong.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "From a hotel bathroom in Beverly Hills, Skye: *everyone i know is in this room* … *none of them is you*"
  }
